      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-white mb-3">ServerHub VPS Review 2026: IronGrid from $5/mo, 9 Datacenters</h1>
      <p class="text-gray-400 text-base">Last updated: August 26, 2026 · 9 min read</p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose prose-invert max-w-none text-gray-300 leading-relaxed space-y-5">

      <p>The VPSTier index of VPS providers leans heavily toward newer budget players (RackNerd, DediRock, HostNOC, Ultahost) and global hyperscalers (Vultr, DigitalOcean, Linode). Today we are adding a 23-year-old US company that takes a different angle: <strong>ServerHub</strong> has been selling IronGrid VPS and IronMetal dedicated servers since 2002, runs 9 verified data centers across the US and Europe, and pairs every VPS plan with a 10 Gbit network port as standard. We pulled the live pricing and specs from serverhub.com, cross-checked the company timeline from the official about page, and compared the lineup against the budget and hyperscaler options we already cover.</p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mt-10 mb-4">ServerHub at a Glance</h2>
      <p>ServerHub launched its initial web hosting brand in 2002, expanded into dedicated server hosting in 2007, and entered the Phoenix market in 2008. By 2013 the company had opened a Dallas facility; Chicago followed in 2015; Frankfurt and Amsterdam came online as the company grew its European footprint. The company ranked <strong>#426 on the Inc 500 in 2014</strong> and <strong>#2017 on the Inc 5000 in 2015</strong> (two consecutive years on the list, verified on the official timeline), and has run an IPv6-native global network since 2011. Today the company sells two VPS product lines — <strong>IronGrid Pure SSD</strong> and <strong>IronGrid SSD-Cached</strong> — alongside a full IronMetal dedicated server catalog. We verified the VPS pricing on the live IronGrid SSD-VPS and SSD-Cached landing pages in August 2026.</p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mt-10 mb-4">The IronGrid Pure SSD line — 8 tiers, $5 to $170/month</h2>
      <p>The headline VPS product is IronGrid Pure SSD: 2 to 8 vCPU cores, 1 to 64 GB RAM, 50 GB to 720 GB of RAID-10 SSD storage, and 1 TB to 20 TB of transfer. Every plan ships on a 10 Gbit network port with full root access, instant virtualization, and a choice of Linux OS templates (Ubuntu, CentOS, and others available at deploy time). The eight verified tiers are:</p>

