      <p>The PRO I entry at $5/mo is competitive on RAM and SSD vs the Vultr $5/mo Cloud Compute tier (1 vCPU + 1 GB + 25 GB SSD) — you get 2 vCPU cores and double the storage, with RAID-10 underneath. The higher tiers include "Cloud Solo" inclusions on the Master II / Starter II / VALUE II plans (per the live page), which bundle cPanel Solo licensing and management hooks. You can verify the live lineup on the official <a href="https://www.serverhub.com/vps/ssd-vps/" class="text-orange-400 hover:underline" rel="noopener" target="_blank">ServerHub IronGrid Pure SSD page</a>.</p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mt-10 mb-4">The IronGrid SSD-Cached line — bulk cache at the same $5 starting point</h2>
      <p>For workloads that prioritize bulk storage over RAM, ServerHub also offers <strong>IronGrid SSD-Cached</strong>: 512 MB to 64 GB RAM, 500 GB to 7 TB of cache-backed storage, and 1 TB to 9 TB of transfer. The entry SSD-Cached plan is $5/mo with 512 MB RAM and 500 GB of storage — a configuration that fits a bulk backup node or small static-content host, but is memory-constrained for general application workloads. The top SSD-Cached tier is 64 GB RAM + 7 TB cache + 9 TB transfer at $140/mo, which undercuts the equivalent Pure SSD VALUE II ($170/mo) for buyers who want more storage than raw RAM. Live lineup on the official <a href="https://www.serverhub.com/vps/ssd-cached/" class="text-orange-400 hover:underline" rel="noopener" target="_blank">ServerHub IronGrid SSD-Cached page</a>.</p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mt-10 mb-4">Network and datacenters — 9 POPs across US + EU</h2>
      <p>ServerHub's <a href="https://www.serverhub.com/network" class="text-orange-400 hover:underline" rel="noopener" target="_blank">network page</a> lists 9 confirmed data centers: Phoenix AZ (PHX-1), Dallas TX (DAL-1 and DAL-2), Chicago IL (CHI-1), Seattle WA (SEA-1), Frankfurt DE (FRA-1), New York NY (NYC-1), Amsterdam NL (AMS-1), and Los Angeles CA (LAX-1). All POPs run on Juniper redundant backbones with Cisco switching fabrics, and ServerHub advertises up to <strong>40 Gbit/s per server and 100 Gbit/s intra-datacenter</strong> connectivity — though the standard VPS product ships at 10 Gbit/s port speed. The company runs full BGP blended transit and claims 100+ direct peering relationships (named peers include Amazon, Facebook, Cox, and Softlayer). IPv6 is native since 2011, with IPv6 included on every service at no extra cost.</p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mt-10 mb-4">Pros and Cons</h2>
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 my-6">
        <div class="bg-[#111] border border-white/5 rounded-2xl p-6">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-green-400 mb-3">Pros</h3>
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-gray-300">
            <li>✅ 10 Gbit/s network port on every VPS plan, scaling to 40 Gbit/s on higher tiers</li>
            <li>✅ 9 verified datacenters across US (7) and EU (2) with Juniper + Cisco backbone</li>
            <li>✅ Pure SSD tier uses RAID-10 storage from $5/mo for verifiable I/O performance</li>
            <li>✅ IPv6-native since 2011 with IPv6 included on every VPS at no extra cost</li>
            <li>✅ 23-year operating track record (founded 2002) with 2× Inc 500 / Inc 5000 appearances</li>
            <li>✅ Instant virtualization deployments with full root access and Linux OS template selection</li>
            <li>✅ 99.999% network uptime SLA with full BGP blended transit and 100+ peering relationships</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#111] border border-white/5 rounded-2xl p-6">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-400 mb-3">Cons</h3>
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-gray-300">
            <li>⚠️ No free in-line DDoS protection listed on VPS product pages (RackNerd/Vultr include it)</li>
            <li>⚠️ 9-DC footprint is mid-size vs Vultr (32+) or DigitalOcean (14) — no APAC or South America</li>
            <li>⚠️ Pure SSD PRO I entry ships only 1 GB RAM — tight beyond a single small site or dev sandbox</li>
            <li>⚠️ SSD-Cached entry is 512 MB RAM / 500 GB cache — memory-constrained for non-trivial workloads</li>
            <li>⚠️ No public hourly billing — VPS plans bill monthly without Vultr-style per-hour spin-up</li>
            <li>⚠️ Lower-tier storage (50 GB / 80 GB SSD on PRO I / Master I) is modest vs the 128 GB+ common at $5 elsewhere</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mt-10 mb-4">How ServerHub compares to RackNerd and Vultr</h2>
      <p>ServerHub is best understood against the two anchors we cover most:</p>
